# Two arms at a disjunctive target writing different alternatives under
# patterns that can hold together: the structs unify into an instance of
# neither, though they share no field.
-- source.cue --
p: bool
-- target.cue --
o: {a: int} | {b: int}
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {
	o: {
		if v0_0.p {a: 1}
		if !v0_0.p {b: 2}
		if v0_0.p {b: 2}
	}
}
-- out --
not total
v1_0.o is written as {...}, an instance of alternative 0 of the target schema's disjunction, and as {...}, an instance of alternative 1, and the two unify into an instance of neither; write the field once per instance (rule write-conflict) @ lens.cue:6:3
